            <ArticleTitle>Torsion of appendices epiploicae presenting as acute abdomen: laparoscopic diagnosis and therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>68-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a 65-year-old man presenting with acute pain in the abdomen. Diagnostic laparoscopy revealed gangrenous torsion in one of the appendices epiploicae in the ascending colon. This was excised with harmonic scalpel.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
